  "question": {
    "text": "If a circle passes through the point $(a, b)$ and cuts the circle $x^2+y^2=4$ orthogonally, then the locus of its centre is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "MCMWb",
      "text": "\n$2 a x+2 b y+\\left(a^2+b^2+4\\right)=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9uY6H",
      "text": "\n$2 a x+2 b y-\\left(a^2+b^2+4\\right)=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "00040",
      "text": "\n$2 a x-2 b y+\\left(a^2+b^2+4\\right)=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VNTA5",
      "text": "\n$2 a x-2 b y-\\left(a^2+b^2+4\\right)=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the circle be $x^2+y^2+2 g x+2 f y+c=0 \\Rightarrow c=4$ and it passes through $(a, b)$ $\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{a}^2+\\mathrm{b}^2+2 \\mathrm{ga}+2 \\mathrm{fb}+4=0$\nHence locus of the centre is $2 a x+2 b y-\\left(a^2+b^2+4\\right)=0$",
    "image": null
  },
